From: Vorapol Rinsatitnon <vorapol.r@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 04 Sep 2026 20:04:27 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] os: open the console devices by the names Windows 7 accepts

Windows 7 reports its console devices as missing. CL 560755 (Go 1.23) added
stat support for them and CL 671458 (Go 1.25) made "not found" a final answer.

	GetFileAttributesEx("CON")  ->  not found
	                            ->  stat gives up before trying CreateFile

	CONIN$  <->  \.\CONIN$      the same console, two names
	Win7    ->   only the bare name can be opened

Treat "not found" for CON, CONIN$ and CONOUT$ as no answer, with or without the
\.\ prefix. This cannot hide a real absence, because these are reserved device
names and no file can exist under one.

The prefixed names reach the console through the object namespace, which the
console devices only join from Windows 8 on. Retry a failed prefixed open with
the bare name, in both stat and openFileNolog, so that Stat and Open agree.


diff --git a/src/os/export_windows_test.go b/src/os/export_windows_test.go
